Playing as a priest for the first time, I've been finding that
locating decent weapons and armor that don't hinder spellcasting has
been the biggest new challenge.  In a recent game I was wandering
around level 8 or 9 with an AC that was far too high when a leucrotta
found me.  Bam! Bam! Bam! and I was down to 13 hit points.  I checked
my inventory for an escape item and saw a cursed scroll of
teleportation.  Figuring that that was just the ticket, I read it.
Unfortunately, it deposited me downward a few levels, right into a Big
Room teeming with monsters.  Luckily, I was close to the upstairs, and
after a few steps in that direction I saw that I would make it if I
could endure a single hit from an E.  I checked it: a fire elemental.
Alas, the alarm bells failed to go off.  It got its one hit in, and I
groaned as several scrolls burst into flame.  Then my potions started
exploding.  One of them turned out to be a potion of paralysis.
DYWYPI?

Next game!  I got down to Minetown, barely, not having found much
worthwhile loot on the way down.  There was an expensive lamp in
Izchak's shop, though, so I bought it and used one of my starting
potions of holy water to bless it.  After a few rubs, a genie popped
out and offered me a wish.  Blessed +2 GDSM, please!  That got my AC
down to -8, by far the best I'd been able to achieve as a priest to
date.  I explored further and found that I was actually on a bones
level.  There was a bunch of uninteresting cursed stuff on the grave,
but also the blessed Excalibur!  That had to be better than my doubly-
eroded starting mace, at least for the time being.  My luck seemed to
be changing!

At about that time I noticed a floating eye had started to follow me
around.  As I exited one of the shops, it was directly south of me.  I
thought "OK, careful now.  Take a step north, then lob some
projectiles south."  On the way to my hands, my instructions somehow
got perverted into "Take a step south."  CRAP!  Now I'm paralyzed.  I
seem to remember in the hazy days of my youth that I occasionally used
to survive a mistake like that, but lately it's been a death
sentence.  Sure enough, a panther showed up and clawed me to death
while I stood there helpless.  My new, better AC only made the
agonized space-bar tapping last longer.

That incident reminded me of my most recent ascension game, when I got
my barbarian down to Moloch's Sanctum, where the priest tossed a
potion of sleep at me.  I could have sworn I'd noshed on some elves at
some point and gotten sleep resistance, but maybe gremlins had stolen
it, because the potion knocked me right out.  The priest came up and
starting beating the crap out of me.  I was utterly horrified as my
hit points dropped, but I finally woke up with twelve points to
spare.  I evaluated my options and hazarded a zap from my wand of
death, which thankfully did the job.  That may be the closest I've
come to having a heart attack playing Nethack.


